Or throw yourself?

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.520
What?

00:00:53.640 --> 00:01:02.300
If you wish to go to the very depths of Ashina then you'd best cast yourself out.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:09.420
It's hard to know what the lives of the ancient Ashina were like, save that they lived on land that was coveted by many.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.629
The gate before this jump is a torii gate,

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.229
which marks the transition from the mundane to the sacred, and the land below is indeed sacred.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:27.029
So sacred, in fact, that the water, rocks and soil here in Mibu Village once attracted the attention of the gods.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.860
One of the gods worshipped here was likely the Serpent God,

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.480
as its skin is found throughout the village, and another was likely Buddha, a

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:42.363
deity friendly with the Serpent God, whose statue can be found desecrated in the main temple.

00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:49.840
Then, far away to the west, some event caused the Sakura Dragon to be cut free from its homeland.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.560
It drifted to the east,

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:56.219
to Japan, where it found the fertile depths of Ashina.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:03.500
Then it settled here, conjuring a divine realm, usurping the lesser gods and tearing the fate of Mibu

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:09.749
Village in half. It seems like a lucky few would have immediately become citizens of the palace,

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:14.958
these nobles, but that also means that most of Mibu had to simply

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:21.000
content themselves with the divine waters that begin flowing through their village. These waters

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.899
bestowed a ton of bounties upon the Mibu, bounties that were distributed throughout all of Ashina;

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:35.000
Dragonspring Sake: a drink that no words can do justice, Mibu Balloons: orbs of water that were sealed

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:40.729
with bountiful prayers, and even Magnificent Medicines: good enough to be stored in this chest,

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:48.199
apparently created by Dogen, the famous doctor. And yet, for all the perks that were offered by its proximity,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.369
the Divine Realm still lay tragically out of reach, until

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:57.889
the Okami Clan arrived in Mibu Village. This group of warrior women,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:06.109
technically called the Kuraokami Clan, were among the first to figure out how to ascend. They did this by

00:03:06.359 --> 00:03:11.269
accruing three ingredients that they knew were stemming from The Fountainhead,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.879
and they created incense with them

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:19.009
The first ingredient was the stem of a sakura tree, for even to this day, a

00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:23.779
sakura blooms in Mibu Village. It might even be an everblossom.

00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:29.479
And the Mibu have prayed with the power of sakura for the longest time.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:36.139
The second ingredient was the fragrance of a flower that thrives in the deepest waters of the Fountainhead.

00:03:36.569 --> 00:03:42.559
They called it a Lotus of the Palace. And lastly, they offered a Shelter Stone,

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:48.679
which is something that grows inside the body of one who has long drank from the fountain headwaters.

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:55.749
It's a lot like these cancer-like grave wax lumps that manifest in all of the undead in the game,

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:02.980
and these Shelter Stone rocks, too, can appear in the bodies of those who drink from these immortal waters.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.510
And wrapped in the Fountainhead Fragrance, the Okami ascended to the palace.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:19.239
